thread:
Maya Chen: Hey team — spotted a weird layout issue on foldable / very-narrow screens in the Console. When the left rail collapses to icons-only, the table's first column (token IDs) sometimes jumps to a new line, the ellipsis shifts into the next column, and keyboard focus gets lost. Screenshot: https://staging.redwood.internal/ux/bug-321.png

Devin Patel: Repro'd on Pixel Fold emulator. Looks like flex-shrink + the sidebar width transition causes a reflow mid-render. I can repro with a 100+ char ID.

Sofia Alvarez: Accessibility nit — focus should remain on the same grid cell after the sidebar toggle. Also VoiceOver reads the truncated cell as just 'more' currently; we should provide an aria-label containing the full text so screen readers get the ID.

Samir Reddy: A couple of ideas: reserve a min-width for the first column and use text-overflow: ellipsis; or clamp() the max-width so it doesn't collapse unpredictably. For mobile, "show on tap" for full text is better than hover.

Maya Chen: Agreed. Also, copy tweak: where we expose a 'Show more' affordance below the truncated ID, prefer 'Copy ID' or an inline copy button — that maps to the most common action.

Devin Patel: Quick CSS POC I'm going to try in staging: 
```css
.table-cell {
  min-width: 120px;
  max-width: clamp(80px, 30vw, 220px);
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.main-area {
  /* disable animated width during collapse to avoid layout thrash */
  transition: none;
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .main-area { transition: width 160ms ease; }
}
```
I'll push as a small hotfix to staging.

Sofia Alvarez: +1 to removing the transition during layout changes — should drop CLS. Keep a subtle animation for the sidebar icon state so users still see affordance. For screen readers, ensure aria-live isn't announcing the entire table when the layout changes.

UI-Bot: Staging build 234 deployed to staging-ux (link: https://ci.redwood/internal/builds/234) :rocket:

Samir Reddy: Perf note — disabling transition avoids layout thrash but we should only do it during the toggle, then re-enable. Also ensure we don't force a layout reflow in JS; prefer CSS-only.

Lina Park: I'll run QA across devices: iPhone SE, Pixel Fold, Chrome narrow emulation, VoiceOver, TalkBack, and keyboard-only nav. Adding this to tomorrow's checklist.

Maya Chen: Assigning to @Devin for patch, @Lina for QA. If the fix looks good, can we push to canary and include a short console note about the behavioural tweak? Also request a visual regression test for 320px and 280px widths.

Devin Patel: On it — PR incoming in a few hours. I'll add visual diffs and a small integration test that asserts the first-column width doesn't drop below 80px.

Sofia Alvarez: Tooltip/copy text suggestion: 'Full ID: <id>' with a tiny 'Copy' button. Keep labels concise for screen readers e.g. aria-label="Full ID: 0x1234... (copy)".

Maya Chen: Thanks all :heart: Let's try to get this into tomorrow's canary so infra can smoke test on foldables.
